<title>FRANCE: Croatia takes CFM engines for Airbus.</title>
<headline>Croatia takes CFM engines for Airbus.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-03-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S.-French aero engine maker CFM International said on Wednesday that Croatia Airlines had selected the CFM56-5B/P engine for its firm order of six Airbus A319 planes and six options on A319/A320/A321.</p>
<p>In a statement CFM said the value of the engine deal was $150 million.</p>
<p>CFM International is a joint-venture of France's SNECMA and GE.</p>
</text>
